[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122768"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/b7e72ce1ab38408f04f3b8d5a228ec0a3632c60086ef0a7abeb7e18af3002e6b.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "eb6fed23-8f2c-5938-b6d6-f384473c7a6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "3a03023a-44c1-5e85-a695-d4df38e41cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "fbb5f7a0-89a8-52b2-88ac-cff52778ed81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "939d871c-b27f-5eb1-8568-428a6a66ec38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "ac7515ce-8776-569a-b631-7ccc1e6ac79f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b699e459-3edc-5384-aa9f-ae389e93eb4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122769/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer-field/choices ["q-122769/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-122769/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-122769/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" "q-122769/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-122769/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122769" :question/id #uuid "325c1c0b-4619-53ae-99d2-1cba6aa74c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122769" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/e41579712730d26c66d9f46f8d978fd51c8efbd76394c094113454e24b3aaff7.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $4:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/849f44d06de55f14811d433f9ccfdd30d47f6a1db1970cdfbfbd6f16be4959b0.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122769/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "123720a7-625b-54ef-afa7-ff47ae3cdf01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" :answer/id #uuid "33984fc4-9e03-5308-b670-89bec4b51ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "7460fb06-39bc-5608-9475-a8a597e7de62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "cd6ee277-bb02-564a-8958-406f8dbeb2b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770/selection/b336fe0bb5249057b2ff0ec170d4f4011a59ade6c56e9a4ab5b5763d0144b9f6" :answer/id #uuid "06f54f7d-7109-5dc8-8345-05ba8c05fa62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57df1786-42ba-5d4e-bd3c-a713cd14bfa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122770/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-122770/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-122770/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" "q-122770/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-122770/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-122770/selection/b336fe0bb5249057b2ff0ec170d4f4011a59ade6c56e9a4ab5b5763d0144b9f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122770" :question/id #uuid "af85269c-7713-5875-ba80-2526a3b9960f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122770" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/69072873cb1f613ee9c2fa4a4caf3dc3409026c2a8310847b1c3dd890cc816d8.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $6:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/d0d9f0fad038f04b6d93920979161694f4e709a31b68083f20e768bf60aa1675.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3\\sqrt{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122770/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "195a7f3d-267c-5df0-ad28-1c8ce4d39285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0b3bf3d5-a4f3-57a2-8291-3c0f937003b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "accaba33-f571-51b6-a889-253355b3a8c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3e956af7-df63-549e-98a7-24c79b7bc0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1992564f-f46f-5ea5-a5ec-e09dea747ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "12b5156e-1434-5720-a491-1bfe4fd40d4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122766/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-122766/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-122766/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-122766/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-122766/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-122766/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122766" :question/id #uuid "cf021e1e-faf4-5f6a-b0a8-f0391048effd" :question/math-academy-id "q-122766" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/1a46390ced6cc52c535f9f48e5e157cea83960caa339e98b23e3b64c93e0ea38.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is a line segment directed along the $y$-axis. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3-(-1)=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122766/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122766"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "fc20499b-2ad7-5309-b6ce-97c8fe704a44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "afc6c891-b2de-5256-aa84-ed1822f7b011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c72de314-358c-5095-b195-5a29b2141ebc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "563d698c-dde5-5e01-8f5e-9d988ed701bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "579b8d90-5335-502b-a13d-775d474faa94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dae23d7b-1c35-51a0-8ebb-0141af05e413" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122767/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-122767/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-122767/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-122767/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-122767/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-122767/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122767" :question/id #uuid "ddead2b2-17bf-51e1-aac4-3b11ab66184f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122767" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/d82f445e19af6e6d343bfab6c082108e945a8feb21caa9b60a2d93da24fc3f6a.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the line segment directed along the $x$-axis. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5-1=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122767/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122767"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843/selection/b8fa57840d74818a0622187d4c282bbc0de8cb17f74d7d65e0c4a989ca0c9d5c" :answer/id #uuid "8ea84020-34fe-5726-9e54-3ebe0546e2a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843/selection/5e16a9bb31b39acf7d4a41be892cea1f3ca504d3f7d84dba0f9091022e371812" :answer/id #uuid "287a7823-a442-5ff0-8de7-934df0f7c054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi +4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843/selection/c2504524716cd00ef228b78ddcf6ef09c2e45cec8ef42f3c273b642ac24f94dd" :answer/id #uuid "0436f059-7cd1-5e0b-8fac-6de104b7ac21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843/selection/27bfebb700f7a8d28e317d57b5581715730e68cbdf44b2e6b30d14fc5f88cf4c" :answer/id #uuid "38fea2b6-ddf9-5b57-b467-aab07ada5044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843/selection/f87f3dfed50d46bc8a5923464b5cc7c2fc1f09511b7cd45cceaa970492c8b9cb" :answer/id #uuid "941a8d0e-3abf-5229-9f6b-f52aff349f5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c001ae3c-006c-5308-bd48-4c732f8ad4ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122843/selection/27bfebb700f7a8d28e317d57b5581715730e68cbdf44b2e6b30d14fc5f88cf4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122843/selection/b8fa57840d74818a0622187d4c282bbc0de8cb17f74d7d65e0c4a989ca0c9d5c" "q-122843/selection/5e16a9bb31b39acf7d4a41be892cea1f3ca504d3f7d84dba0f9091022e371812" "q-122843/selection/c2504524716cd00ef228b78ddcf6ef09c2e45cec8ef42f3c273b642ac24f94dd" "q-122843/selection/27bfebb700f7a8d28e317d57b5581715730e68cbdf44b2e6b30d14fc5f88cf4c" "q-122843/selection/f87f3dfed50d46bc8a5923464b5cc7c2fc1f09511b7cd45cceaa970492c8b9cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122843" :question/id #uuid "80df4b56-40e8-5fe9-9726-cce3c7cc75c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122843" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/d7844777c0bb540ba337756f45c4d71a8a8e9f9c84372e01542892801efecce3.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/98f444851e2df505d4242d1f8e4be0d76f78babd5d9633d9ab0ec84c245fe364.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is three-quarters of a circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{3}{4}(2\\pi r)=3\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3\\pi +2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122843/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e60b3dd1-0842-562d-a72f-5adb6a60cba8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122843"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122481"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/558dbbc424725ca0d9bad628968489cc2e32d67136102290666ff055a634bc16.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/82fedadbb33b1747832bac25d9cda8e0b6b18b0fab411a870e90bc09ce47226e.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a semi-circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\pi r=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4=2(\\pi +2).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "01926086-4531-51f4-ac0f-6a59371b1169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "edd730ad-b3be-5096-a165-233ad0289287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "5f73e647-e40d-5eec-9d33-4da67adacba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "b1290eb8-cefa-5a26-a0b2-a1498fd6068a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "be9c52fe-d752-5698-bd06-b011753fc545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5850c0fc-03ca-537b-9cea-9ab26ce1f0d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122828/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-122828/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-122828/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-122828/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-122828/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-122828/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122828" :question/id #uuid "f4276705-6aa2-5565-947d-f686c87d0cd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122828" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/39a7cb0b31cb5d906803063597ae968be8fba90f048a4d9745225de7c3f8d6db.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/058c7b33112329df321e61660df4f2d388f42ca40c0aae5b73a089a0251726e2.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe paths ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are line segments of length $3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3+5+3=11.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e60b3dd1-0842-562d-a72f-5adb6a60cba8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850/selection/e2205d4380220e2ed66b9d3b7145a241f4ae6dc8f468d390aca06ddd4e479a00" :answer/id #uuid "2fa6c612-f3e2-5622-a20d-d14547a6abcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850/selection/652c81f324cddbd6f037211672d2059608a38eee1018466d45d33d18a9ca5d8d" :answer/id #uuid "b8909c63-ceb4-5c55-8440-e72da28c2d88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(2\\pi +\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850/selection/82ee0468934cf50f19b4ae35d2dfc7ab9935ba40e361320c62cd48d73016e3ea" :answer/id #uuid "2fedd427-c97f-5fa2-98b0-c2ca918ef2e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850/selection/d7c53a4e7adaadb018f4104e099f5b980677a4a9074c0cbd1bac325d5d53cf2c" :answer/id #uuid "4c3e7afb-b7a5-52a8-96cf-477e9d3feff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850/selection/11ef0070240ea05ce9f3597d5658fd10ea5b7691b6460af0b2f60d87adffee5a" :answer/id #uuid "befb6801-2837-51de-9934-f8a0f4f8bee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbdc4de7-4d4c-520e-8524-9b0e3ae515ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122850/selection/11ef0070240ea05ce9f3597d5658fd10ea5b7691b6460af0b2f60d87adffee5a" :answer-field/choices ["q-122850/selection/e2205d4380220e2ed66b9d3b7145a241f4ae6dc8f468d390aca06ddd4e479a00" "q-122850/selection/652c81f324cddbd6f037211672d2059608a38eee1018466d45d33d18a9ca5d8d" "q-122850/selection/82ee0468934cf50f19b4ae35d2dfc7ab9935ba40e361320c62cd48d73016e3ea" "q-122850/selection/d7c53a4e7adaadb018f4104e099f5b980677a4a9074c0cbd1bac325d5d53cf2c" "q-122850/selection/11ef0070240ea05ce9f3597d5658fd10ea5b7691b6460af0b2f60d87adffee5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122850" :question/id #uuid "86bf6c2c-defc-5c47-a3d1-c7d99add5f71" :question/math-academy-id "q-122850" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/bf87c4707c0f4a8ab1b5157a13e8c7785da915833c5f9d896a2747af27f70e59.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/ff52b8e83a9cc9867b25ea3c24ed0f988a27dec73f9e0ab2dfda28ddabb3238a.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}=2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122850/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e60b3dd1-0842-562d-a72f-5adb6a60cba8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122850"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845/selection/060ad5da6ebf9bb43cf04e60d4e5cc8ce4232f1bca8cf1f25fe8319021bbb363" :answer/id #uuid "e331d612-9168-5ac4-911d-eefdc7b69a28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(3+\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "cb1b6ee4-41ca-5e93-8049-46c46004fdcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845/selection/06cb10a650d14a8983cd37bdd31fec3c81902606450ab40460c7c78eb0e13eb4" :answer/id #uuid "25cf667f-4eac-538b-8986-8d4c02956725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5+2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845/selection/09069ac2d5ba22f0768c13cd9404d1c2016de05818bbd47f5824fb3015a1ab1a" :answer/id #uuid "0cca7cee-927e-5e51-97ae-c2f9f11fda07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(2+\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "0d5bd321-845e-57b6-8d39-8d7efe1085f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a71c9b66-3984-5ce2-84e9-16997a12ff54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122845/selection/06cb10a650d14a8983cd37bdd31fec3c81902606450ab40460c7c78eb0e13eb4" :answer-field/choices ["q-122845/selection/060ad5da6ebf9bb43cf04e60d4e5cc8ce4232f1bca8cf1f25fe8319021bbb363" "q-122845/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-122845/selection/06cb10a650d14a8983cd37bdd31fec3c81902606450ab40460c7c78eb0e13eb4" "q-122845/selection/09069ac2d5ba22f0768c13cd9404d1c2016de05818bbd47f5824fb3015a1ab1a" "q-122845/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122845" :question/id #uuid "eae17276-a088-564f-b102-c6a2bb769280" :question/math-academy-id "q-122845" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/68b3f78c29c9d7776efc2a78672ae53fe2e806d7ca6c3d663de8a16c03342132.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/27c19b56a24315f1105539afc441a33957dddf606b3410b86121e7cb8ed16973.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5+2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122845/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e60b3dd1-0842-562d-a72f-5adb6a60cba8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "1b184b9f-b217-556c-8b33-e5ae1142794a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "33201e7e-23e1-5f63-9641-06ff5682e032" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "fd0da72a-0e55-585d-ac97-ef2412fc558c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0f13ff9f-d65a-511d-b0b9-1f82fb9dd65a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1b07dc0a-5454-5714-a318-baaecae6710b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7cc522-1a3c-5573-b70a-f313e7a4fd67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122816/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-122816/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-122816/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-122816/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122816/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-122816/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122816" :question/id #uuid "a0ee2acf-324d-5412-b01f-2421ba3682e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-122816" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 4.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3$\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-3$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=12,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨4u,\\,8{u}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3/2},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122816/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122816"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4862e573-148f-5aed-8dcf-73c53200aa38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "469cd30e-60db-5f93-98e4-e4afdd9b5617" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "7eab524e-e812-58ca-ab89-b8689791c9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bd7cbb71-f657-5598-8845-3be0edccf2e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c76e721e-082c-5802-9e1e-53007adb799a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "faee87d2-ea2d-5a97-b570-bd79d72eaa86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122868/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-122868/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-122868/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-122868/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122868/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-122868/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122868" :question/id #uuid "5ca5e59f-c106-581f-9ebe-3d7ecb79439a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122868" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨2t,\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 2 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨4u,\\,2\\sqrt{2u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2k$\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2x},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122868/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "87493a09-01cf-5e0f-abeb-6b6030e73069" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1b46af28-d545-5444-a891-9d71de90793a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2ce3bb0a-e473-5af6-9bb8-1958785efac9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9d50c880-12a2-5cc7-99ff-f6cbb365654c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a7c48ee8-1248-5d89-9da9-2d9249e1f9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "048cc43f-95ae-5086-a05f-0545a0f79471" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122815/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122815/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-122815/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-122815/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122815/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122815/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122815" :question/id #uuid "751a2612-5884-5a0e-995e-cbb5f375d2f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-122815" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(u)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{u}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{u}{2})⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2\\pi .$ \n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\pi .$\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we note that both parameterizations traverse a half-circle of radius $1$ centered at $O$ between $0$ and $\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122815/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122815"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bd4dd718-acd1-5774-ac4a-49915a8443da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3852ac79-4729-51f8-805d-bfe694475237" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a5f57b57-688b-5c56-a764-79bd1b79cc5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "548b7aff-51e9-5ba9-b465-ced3e7c97858" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "add131cc-01c7-5ecf-8c1e-8b7dccb11072" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f85bffd2-e183-5912-8de1-0a4b30dc4f6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122814/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122814/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-122814/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122814/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122814/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-122814/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122814" :question/id #uuid "91efdf57-0580-5a7a-8027-92d6b70a8e32" :question/math-academy-id "q-122814" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 2.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=8,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨16{u}^{4}-12{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false, while statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx={y}^{4}-3{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122814/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122814"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4b292f67-ccab-5680-8ca0-b5e89271d6f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1b6d2dbd-f3a1-534c-bc3d-e3afdd57dfb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "77538e54-efcf-52a8-bc3f-34e8988e0973" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ad16d190-f774-5dba-a605-49c0d3bc94f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "190c6185-b84e-5dc3-a521-0f5538099385" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce3456ae-c54a-5308-bcbd-dde21603b95d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122851/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122851/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122851/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-122851/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122851/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-122851/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122851" :question/id #uuid "714b1c37-82c2-52dc-8892-8df8ef438e81" :question/math-academy-id "q-122851" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+1},\\,3t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+1},\\,2u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{3}$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1},\\,0\\le y\\le 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122851/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122851"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9470"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/765415456d7f33c3558e08e7c4fc01ef3e80961c1e073a210033d91741d78f60.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s,$ where $C$ is the arc of a semicircle of radius $4$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $C$ is a semicircle of radius $r = 4.$ Its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L=\\pi r=4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = 4\\pi.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9471"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/84de7754ed9244e3d646e452f6ed6dab349c130d17eae1d4dbc94cb52bd761e1.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above, traversed once counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/f4e80a23910612bd55e7578a074f23c76535139889faff479c4dd0521e7496ff.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C = C_1 \\cup C_2 \\cup C_3$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s =  \\int_{C_1}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s + \\int_{C_2}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s + \\int_{C_3}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nThe path $C_1$ is a semicircle of radius $r = 3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} \\,\\textrm ds = \\dfrac{1}{2}(2 \\pi r) = 3\\pi.\n$$\n\nThe paths $C_2$ and $C_3$ are hypotenuses of right triangles whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} \\,\\textrm ds = \\int_{C_3} \\,\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = 5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = 3\\pi + 5 + 5 = 3\\pi + 10.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9472"] :question/problem "Consider the curves $C_1$ and $C_2,$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{3},\\,t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨3{u}^{3},\\,3u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $\\displaystyle\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = 3k$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Notice that $C_1$ and $C_2$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that $C_1$ and $C_2$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{1}{9}y^3, \\quad 0\\leq y\\leq 3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds  = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
